Register cleanup immediately after creating the handle, so it runs even if an assertion fails:

```dart
testWidgets('accessibility', (tester) async {
  final handle = tester.ensureSemantics();
  addTearDown(handle.dispose);

  await tester.pumpWidget(const MyApp());
  await expectLater(tester, meetsGuideline(textContrastGuideline));
});
```

Remove the trailing `handle.dispose()`. If the extra handle isn’t needed, remove it entirely: `testWidgets` enables semantics by default and cleans up its own handle.
